---
import Paragraph from './AnimationReadingParagraph.astro';
import Text from './AnimationReadingText.astro';
import '../styles/editorial-review.css';
const {story,route}=Astro.props;
const sourceMap=new Map(story.sources.map(s=>[s.id,s]));
const refs=(item)=> (item.sourceIds||item.source_ids||[]).map(id=>{const s=sourceMap.get(id);if(!s)throw new Error(`Unknown source ${id}`);return s;});
const chapters=[{href:'/wallet/history',title:'Wallet history'},{href:'/wallet/future',title:'Future wallets'},{href:'/marketplace/history',title:'Marketplace history'},{href:'/zed-run',title:'ZED retrospective'}];
const isZed=story.theme==='zed';
const diagramNotes={
 'wallet-stack':['The requesting app proposes an action; it does not gain signing authority merely by asking.','The connection channel carries requests and account information. It is distinct from the signer.','Wallet review interprets a request and applies policy; a familiar screen alone is not evidence of safety.','The signer authorizes according to its device, key or quorum rules.','The network validates and records. A returned receipt is observable state, not control over a key.'],
 'permission-ladder':['Connection shares account information; disconnecting removes that connection.','A message signature may carry meaningful authority even without an immediate network fee.','An allowance authorizes a named spender up to a limit; disconnecting does not revoke it.','Broad account authority is delegated to code and can persist until changed. The authorization tuple supplies no granular spending limit; limits depend on the implementation.'],
 'recovery-map':['A recovery root and the correct account derivation are distinct from a local app password.','Kukai’s published legacy DirectAuth architecture uses OAuth/Torus-mediated key access; it is not guardian recovery.','The hardware device controls signing. Its recovery dependencies remain separate from the display app.'],
 'account-abstraction':['A UserOperation is not itself a regular network transaction.','A bundler assembles operations; it is not the chain’s validator.','EntryPoint coordinates the specified validation and execution path.','Actual account features depend on the implementation.','An EOA authorizes a code designation under EIP-7702.','Delegated code executes in EOA context; designation persists until changed.'],
 'network-support':['The interface decides what it displays.','A supported network has a compatible interface path.','Removing support changes the app, not the separate network’s history.','Continued access requires a compatible control and recovery path.']
};
---
<article class:list={['ed','wallet-editorial',story.theme]}>
 <a class="skip" href="#complete-reading">Skip to the complete reading</a>
 <header class="mast"><a href="/">POINTCAST</a><nav aria-label="Related readings">{chapters.filter(c=>c.href!==route).map(c=><a href={c.href}>{c.title}</a>)}<a href="/wallet">Collector view</a><a href="/ues">UES</a></nav></header>
 <header class:list={['hero',{'zed-hero':isZed}]}>
  {isZed&&<img class="hero-art" src={story.images[0].src} alt={story.images[0].alt} width={story.images[0].width} height={story.images[0].height} fetchpriority="high" />}
  <div class="hero-copy"><p class="kicker">PointCast / {isZed?'Digital worlds':story.theme==='marketplace'?'Markets and culture':'Wallet field guide'} / checked {story.checkedDate}</p><h1>{story.title}</h1><p class="dek">{story.dek}</p>{story.subtitle&&<p>{story.subtitle}</p>}</div>
 </header>
 {isZed&&<p class="art-caption">{story.images[0].caption}</p>}
 <p class="note scope">{story.scopeNote}</p>
 <nav class="jump" aria-label="Reading contents">{story.sections.map(s=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{s.heading}</a>)}{story.cases&&<a href="#cases">Three wallet cases</a>}{story.timeline&&<a href="#timeline">Chronology</a>}{story.diagrams&&<a href="#diagrams">Technical maps</a>}{story.statusCards&&<a href="#status">Capability status</a>}{story.decisions&&<a href="#decisions">Decision guide</a>}{story.permissionLab&&<a href="#permission-lab">Permission Lab</a>}{(story.exercises||story.ues)&&<a href="#practice">UES practice</a>}{story.business&&<a href="#business">IndustryNext</a>}<a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
 <div id="complete-reading">{story.sections.map(s=><section class="prose" id={s.id}><h2>{s.heading}</h2>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><Paragraph text={p}/>)}<p class="source-ref">Sources: {refs(s).map(source=><a href={source.url}>{source.title} ↗ </a>)}</p></section>)}</div>
 {story.cases&&<section id="cases"><p class="kicker">Three current product cases / checked {story.checkedDate}</p><h2>Same questions. Different control models.</h2>{story.cases.map(c=><details class="case"><summary><strong>{c.title}</strong><span>{c.dek}</span></summary><div>{c.sections.map(s=><section class="prose" id={s.id}><h3>{s.heading}</h3>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><Paragraph text={p}/>)}<p class="source-ref">Sources: {refs(s).map(source=><a href={source.url}>{source.title} ↗ </a>)}</p></section>)}</div></details>)}</section>}
 {story.theme==='marketplace'&&<section class="prose concept"><p class="kicker">Original conceptual map</p><h2>The marketplace has six dependencies.</h2><ol class="node-grid">{['Token contract','Orders','Settlement','Indexer','Media storage','Rights / license'].map((n,i)=><li><span class="kicker">Layer {i+1}</span><strong>{n}</strong></li>)}</ol><p>A surviving token contract does not establish continued orders, search, media availability or reproduction rights. These layers are conceptual, not an audited system topology.</p><p class="source-ref">Follow the section-level sources above for each platform’s dated implementation and status.</p></section>}
 {story.timeline&&<section class="prose" id="timeline"><h2>A dated chronology.</h2><ol class="timeline">{story.timeline.map(t=><li><p class="kicker">{t.date}</p>{t.title&&<h3>{t.title}</h3>}<Text text={t.description}/><p class="source-ref">{refs(t).map(s=><a href={s.url}>{s.title} ↗ </a>)}</p></li>)}</ol></section>}
 {story.diagrams&&<section id="diagrams"><p class="kicker">Original teaching diagrams</p><h2>Inspect the mechanism.</h2>{story.diagrams.map(d=><section class="diagram prose" aria-labelledby={d.id}><h3 id={d.id}>{d.title}</h3><p>{d.caption}</p><div class="node-grid">{d.nodes.map((node,i)=><details class:list={{'broad-authority':d.id==='permission-ladder'&&i===3}}><summary><span class="kicker">{i+1}</span><strong>{node}</strong>{d.id==='permission-ladder'&&i===3&&<span class="authority-label">Broad account authority</span>}</summary><p>{diagramNotes[d.id][i]}</p></details>)}</div>{d.edges&&<div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Permanent text equivalent: request and state paths</caption><thead><tr><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>{d.edges.map(edge=><tr><td>{edge.from}</td><td>{edge.to}</td><td>{edge.label}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>}<p class="source-ref">Sources: {refs(d).map(s=><a href={s.url}>{s.title} ↗ </a>)}</p></section>)}</section>}
 {story.statusCards&&<section id="status"><p class="kicker">Dated evidence / checked {story.checkedDate}</p><h2>Shipped, documented, draft or proposed?</h2><div class="status-grid">{story.statusCards.map(card=><article><p class="kicker">{card.label}</p><h3>{card.title}</h3><p>{card.detail}</p><p class="source-ref">{refs(card).map(s=><a href={s.url}>{s.title} ↗ </a>)}</p></article>)}</div></section>}
 {story.decisions&&<section class="prose" id="decisions"><h2>Seven questions before choosing a tool.</h2>{story.decisions.map(d=><details class="decision"><summary>{d.question}</summary><p>{d.look_for}</p></details>)}</section>}
 {story.permissionLab&&<section class="prose permission-lab" id="permission-lab"><p class="kicker">SIMULATION / fictional identifiers only</p><h2>Disconnect is different from revoke.</h2><p>A fictional gallery sees PC-PLAYER and has an allowance of 20 PRACTICE-TICKET units. Toggle the two independent permissions to inspect the result. This panel changes only the labels below.</p><fieldset><legend>Fictional permission state</legend><label><input type="checkbox" data-lab-connect checked /> Gallery connection</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-lab-allowance checked /> Spender allowance</label></fieldset><output aria-live="polite" data-lab-output>Connected; allowance remains 20 practice tickets.</output><p class="note">Reading model: disconnecting ends the connection; revoking an allowance is a separate operation. No wallet discovery, network request, signature or transaction occurs.</p><p class="source-ref">{['disconnect','erc20'].map(id=><a href={sourceMap.get(id).url}>{sourceMap.get(id).title} ↗ </a>)}</p></section>}
 {isZed&&<section class="prose zed-teaching"><p class="kicker">Synthetic teaching example</p><h2>A past record is not a next-race probability.</h2><div class="twenty" aria-label="Synthetic record: four wins in twenty starts">{Array.from({length:20},(_,i)=><span class:list={{won:i<4}}>{i<4?'W':'·'}</span>)}</div><dl class="stat-grid"><div><dt>Starts</dt><dd>20</dd></div><div><dt>Wins</dt><dd>4</dd></div><div><dt>Observed win rate</dt><dd>20%</dd></div><div><dt>Next-race probability</dt><dd>Unknown</dd></div></dl><p class="note">Fictional data. No actual stable, horse, measured performance or wagering forecast.</p><figure><img src={story.images[1].src} alt={story.images[1].alt} width={story.images[1].width} height={story.images[1].height} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{story.images[1].caption}</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={story.images[2].src} alt={story.images[2].alt} width={story.images[2].width} height={story.images[2].height} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{story.images[2].caption}</figcaption></figure></section>}
 {story.business&&<section class="prose" id="business"><p class="kicker">IndustryNext / original business analysis</p><h2>What does the model sustain?</h2><p>{story.business.thesis}</p><ul>{story.business.questions.map(q=><li>{q}</li>)}</ul><p class="note">{story.business.interpretation}</p></section>}
 {(story.exercises||story.ues)&&<section class="prose" id="practice"><p class="kicker">University of El Segundo / self-guided practice</p><h2>{story.ues?.module_title||'Read, map and question.'}</h2><p>{story.ues?.description||'UES is an independent community-learning initiative, not an accredited institution or degree program.'}</p>{story.ues&&<ul>{story.ues.learning_outcomes.map(o=><li>{o}</li>)}</ul>}{(story.exercises||story.ues.exercises).map((e,i)=><article class="exercise"><p class="kicker">Exercise {i+1} / {e.minutes||e.estimated_minutes} minutes</p><h3>{e.title}</h3>{e.objective&&<p>{e.objective}</p>}<p>{e.prompt}</p>{e.mock_data&&<dl>{Object.entries(e.mock_data).map(([key,value])=><div><dt>{key}</dt><dd>{String(value)}</dd></div>)}</dl>}{e.deliverable&&<p><strong>Make:</strong> {e.deliverable}</p>}{e.safety&&<p class="note">{e.safety}</p>}{e.answer&&<details><summary>Compare your reasoning</summary><p>{e.answer}</p><ul>{e.rubric.map(r=><li>{r}</li>)}</ul></details>}<p class="source-ref">{refs(e).map(s=><a href={s.url}>{s.title} ↗ </a>)}</p></article>)}{story.ues&&<p class="note">{story.ues.completion_rule}</p>}</section>}
 <section id="sources"><h2>Follow the evidence.</h2><ol class="sources">{story.sources.map(s=><li id={'source-'+s.id}><a href={s.url}>{s.title} ↗</a><small>{s.date||'See source for date'} · checked {story.checkedDate}</small>{s.note&&<p>{s.note}</p>}{s.limitations&&<p class="note">{s.limitations}</p>}</li>)}</ol><details class="prose"><summary>Editorial verification and limits</summary><ul>{story.notes.map(note=><li>{note}</li>)}</ul></details></section>
 <footer>PointCast / Original researched reading. <a href="#complete-reading">Return to the complete story ↑</a></footer>
</article>
<script>
for(const lab of document.querySelectorAll('.permission-lab')){
 const connect=lab.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-lab-connect]');
 const allowance=lab.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-lab-allowance]');
 const output=lab.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>('[data-lab-output]');
 const update=()=>{if(connect&&allowance&&output)output.textContent=`${connect.checked?'Connected':'Disconnected'}; ${allowance.checked?'allowance remains 20 practice tickets':'allowance revoked in this simulation'}.`;};
 connect?.addEventListener('change',update);allowance?.addEventListener('change',update);
}
</script>
<style>
.wallet-editorial{--accent:#237e83}.broad-authority{grid-column:1/-1;background:#fbe9d7;border-width:3px!important}.authority-label{display:block;font-weight:700;color:#8a351a;margin-top:.5rem}.skip{display:inline-block;padding:.8rem 0}.wallet-editorial .mast nav{flex-wrap:wrap}.wallet-editorial .hero{display:block}.wallet-editorial .hero h1{max-width:17ch}.scope{max-width:85ch}.wallet-editorial .prose{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.wallet-editorial :is(a,summary,input):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:5px}.wallet-editorial summary{min-height:44px;cursor:pointer;padding:.8rem 0}.case,.decision,.diagram,.exercise{border:2px solid #15253a;padding:1rem;margin-block:1.2rem}.case summary strong{display:block;font-size:1.6rem}.case summary span{display:block;margin-top:.5rem}.case .prose{margin-block:1.5rem}.node-grid,.status-grid,.stat-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.node-grid{list-style:none;padding:0}.node-grid>*,.status-grid>article{border:2px solid #15253a;padding:1rem;box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #15253a}.node-grid strong{display:block}.timeline{list-style:none;border-left:2px solid var(--accent);padding:0}.timeline>li{padding:0 0 1.5rem 1.5rem}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-block:1rem}caption{text-align:left;font-weight:700}th,td{padding:.6rem;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa}fieldset label{display:block;padding:.8rem;min-height:44px}input{width:1.2rem;height:1.2rem;margin-right:.6rem}output{display:block;border:2px solid var(--accent);padding:1rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:1rem}.exercise dl>div{display:flex;gap:1rem}.exercise dd{margin:0}.wallet-editorial figure{margin:2rem 0}.wallet-editorial figure img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.wallet-editorial figcaption,.art-caption{font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;padding:.7rem 0}.zed{--accent:#78e3f2;background:#11151b;color:#f2f4f7;padding:1.5rem}.zed a{color:#9fe6ee}.zed .note{color:#c8d2de;background:#1d2630;border-color:#788d9b}.zed .kicker{color:#aae8f0}.zed .zed-hero{position:relative;isolation:isolate;min-height:clamp(450px,48vw,730px);display:flex;align-items:center;padding:2rem}.hero-art{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;z-index:-1}.zed-hero:after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(0,0,0,.84),rgba(0,0,0,.45) 43%,transparent 78%);z-index:-1}.zed .hero-copy{max-width:52%}.zed h1{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4vw,4.5rem);color:#fff}.zed .dek{color:#e7f0f7}.zed .exercise,.zed .stat-grid>div{border-color:#73d7e5}.twenty{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(10,1fr);gap:.3rem}.twenty span{text-align:center;padding:.5rem;background:#252d39;color:#c4cdd7}.twenty .won{background:#a6edc8;color:#081711}.stat-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);margin-block:1rem}.stat-grid>div{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid}.stat-grid dd{margin:.5rem 0;font-size:1.25rem}.wallet{background:#fff7df;color:#15253a}.wallet .hero{border:2px solid #15253a;box-shadow:8px 8px 0 #15253a;padding:1.5rem}.wallet h1{font-family:monospace}.wallet .kicker{color:#237e83}.marketplace .concept{border-block:2px solid #15253a;padding-block:2rem}@media(max-width:760px){.node-grid,.status-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.stat-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.zed{padding:1rem}.zed .hero-copy{max-width:100%}.zed .zed-hero{padding:1rem;min-height:560px;align-items:flex-start}.zed-hero:after{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(0,0,0,.87),rgba(0,0,0,.7) 60%,rgba(0,0,0,.25))}.hero-art{object-position:65% center}.case,.diagram,.exercise{padding:.8rem}.wallet .hero{box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #15253a}.twenty{grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr)}}
</style>
